    question: "A section of the small intestine shows the lamina propria containing numerous plasma cells that stain for IgA. These IgA-producing plasma cells are found just beneath the intestinal epithelium. Describe the complete transcytosis pathway by which secretory IgA (sIgA) reaches the intestinal lumen.",
